# Line endings.
#
# These files are read or executed on the Ubuntu VM, where the line endings decide
# whether they work at all:
#
#   * a CRLF in a shebang makes the script fail to start — the kernel looks for an
#     interpreter literally named "/usr/bin/env bash\r";
#   * a CRLF in a sudoers rule can break parsing, and sudoers failing to parse locks
#     out sudo entirely;
#   * the nginx server block, the generated mode include and the systemd unit are all
#     line-oriented configuration.
#
# Pinning them to LF means a checkout on any platform produces bytes the VM can use,
# rather than depending on each contributor's core.autocrlf.
* text=auto

*.sh        text eol=lf
*.py        text eol=lf
*.service   text eol=lf
*.inc       text eol=lf

# These carry no extension, so they are named explicitly.
inauguration/deploy/nginx/nss                   text eol=lf
inauguration/deploy/sudoers/nss-inauguration    text eol=lf
inauguration/deploy/sbin/nss-decommission       text eol=lf

# Binary assets: never touch them.
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.png   binary
*.JPG   binary
*.docx  binary
